    "title": "‘Walker Texas Ranger’ Star Chuck Norris Dies at 86 - The New York Times",
    "text": "new video loaded: ‘Walker Texas Ranger’ Star Chuck Norris Dies at 86transcript‘Walker Texas Ranger’ Star Chuck Norris Dies at 86The family of Chuck Norris announced that the action movie star died on Thursday after he had been hospitalized for a medical emergency earlier that day. Norris was known for his martial arts skills and his role in the CBS television series, “Walker, Texas Ranger.” He was 86.“You know, getting a chance to work with friends I’ve known for over 30 years — Arnold, Sly, and Van Damme and Bruce Willis. I said this would probably be the only time I’d ever get to work with all of them at one time. So that’s why I did it.” “I want to introduce you to the Secretary of Defense, Chuck Norris.”Watch Today’s VideosMore in Obituaries ›Former F.B.I. Director Robert Mueller Dies at 812:01The Powerful Speeches of Jesse Jackson1:55Jesse Jackson Dies at 841:43‘Dawson’s Creek’ Heartthrob James Van Der Beek Dies at 481:04Tatiana Schlossberg, of Kennedy Family, Dies at 350:55Frank O. Gehry, Formidable Architect, Dies at 960:34Video ›Today's VideosU.S.PoliticsImmigrationNY RegionScienceBusinessCultureBooksWellnessWorldAfricaAmericasAsiaSouth AsiaDonald TrumpMiddle East CrisisRussia-Ukraine CrisisVisual InvestigationsOpinion VideoAdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENT",
